## 7. Data Sources and Data Quality

| Data needed | Primary source | Secondary or cross-check | Reliability note |
|---|---|---|---|
| Company financials and filings | SEC EDGAR (10-K, 10-Q, 8-K); company investor relations pages | Yahoo Finance; Nasdaq company pages | Primary filings are the authoritative record. Aggregators may adjust or restate. |
| Sector valuation and earnings aggregates | FactSet Earnings Insight (free weekly report) | S&P Dow Jones Indices; ETF issuer fact sheets | Check each source's definition of "forward" and index membership. |
| Interest rates, inflation, growth | FRED (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis) | US Treasury; BLS; BEA; Federal Reserve statements | Official data, but later revised. Record the release date. |
| Prices and technical indicators | TradingView or StockCharts; Yahoo Finance (adjusted close) | ETF issuer price history | Use dividend-adjusted prices for return calculations. |
| Semiconductor industry data | Semiconductor Industry Association (SIA) and WSTS monthly sales | Company results; SEMI equipment data | Monthly figures are published with a lag. |
| Business activity | ISM Manufacturing PMI | S&P Global PMI | Survey-based; treat as directional. |
| Sentiment | Cboe VIX via FRED; AAII Investor Sentiment Survey | Fund flow summaries from ETF providers | Noisy; use only to confirm other evidence. |
| Qualitative context | Federal Reserve statements; company earnings call transcripts and presentations | Reputable financial media; brokerage research summaries | Opinions vary. Prefer primary documents and note any conflict of interest. |

*Table 6. Data sources.*

### 7.1 Data quality protocol

- Verify every key figure against at least two independent sources, or against the primary filing.
- Record the retrieval date, source, metric definition and series code in a data log for every dataset.
- Use consistent date ranges and dividend-adjusted prices across all calculations.
- Save a raw snapshot of each dataset before any cleaning so that results can be reproduced.
- Distinguish clearly between facts, estimates and opinions in the final write-up.

