## 10. Scenario Framework

Scenarios turn the analysis into a view of the next 6 to 12 months. The triggers below are the conditions that the monitoring plan will watch. They are a framework for reasoning and not a forecast or a statement of probability.

| Scenario | Narrative | Indicator conditions that would support it | What it would imply for the sector |
|---|---|---|---|
| Bull | AI spending continues to convert into earnings; rates stable or easing; breadth widens. | Positive and rising EPS revisions; capex guidance maintained or raised; real yields flat or falling; more stocks above 200-day average. | Trend continuation; valuation supported by earnings growth. |
| Base | Growth continues but at a slower pace; valuation absorbs news without large re-rating. | Revisions flat to mildly positive; capex growth moderating; yields range-bound; leadership narrow. | Choppy, range-bound performance with wide dispersion between stocks. |
| Bear | AI spending slows or fails to earn adequate returns; rates rise or policy shock occurs. | Falling revisions; cuts in capex guidance; real yields rising; weakening breadth; VIX spike. | Valuation compression and drawdown, most severe in the most expensive and most AI-exposed names. |

*Table 8. Scenario framework.*

