## 11. Potential Challenges and Proposed Solutions

| Challenge | Why it matters | Proposed solution |
|---|---|---|
| Information overload and conflicting opinions | Large volumes of commentary with opposing views can lead to cherry-picking. | Anchor on primary data. Pre-define indicators and thresholds before reading commentary. Log opposing views and explain why they are accepted or rejected. |
| Hype and narrative bias | AI is a dominant story, which may bias both sources and the analyst. | Apply the confirmation rule (three of five categories must agree). Explicitly search for evidence that contradicts the working view. |
| Concentration distorts averages | A few mega-cap stocks can make the sector look stronger or weaker than the typical stock. | Report both cap-weighted and equal-weighted results; track breadth and the top-five versus rest comparison. |
| Data revisions and publication lags | Economic data is revised and industry data is delayed, so a snapshot can mislead. | Time-stamp all data. Use the release date, not the period date, when relating data to prices. Note when figures are preliminary. |
| Limits of free data | Free sources may lack estimates history or constituent-level detail. | Use the free FactSet weekly report, ETF issuer data and company filings. Where history is unavailable, state the limitation and use a shorter window. |
| Unstable statistical relationships | Correlations between rates and tech stocks change across market regimes. | Use rolling windows rather than a single full-sample figure; report ranges and avoid over-precise claims. |
| Accounting differences across companies | Adjusted earnings and stock-based compensation can make profits look different across firms. | Compare both GAAP and adjusted measures; use free cash flow as a cross-check. |
| Time constraint | The scope is broad for 32 hours. | Follow the phase budget in Section 9; prioritise the core indicators first; use the three-hour buffer only for the highest-priority gaps. |
| Unexpected events | Policy or geopolitical shocks can invalidate a view quickly. | Maintain the scenario triggers and monitoring calendar; revise the base case when a trigger is hit. |

*Table 9. Challenges and mitigation.*

