## Appendix A: Indicator Scorecard Template

Each category is scored -1 (negative), 0 (neutral) or +1 (positive) against thresholds fixed before the data is examined. The composite is the weighted sum, ranging from -1 to +1. The weights are initial judgements and are shown so that they can be challenged and tested for sensitivity.

| Category | Indicators used | Weight | Example threshold for +1 / -1 | Score |
|---|---|:-:|---|---|
| Valuation | Forward P/E percentile; premium to S&P 500 | 20% | +1: below 40th percentile of 10-year range. -1: above 85th percentile. | To be completed |
| Earnings | EPS growth; revision breadth; capex guidance | 25% | +1: revisions positive and rising. -1: revisions negative. | To be completed |
| Rates and macro | 10-year real yield trend; PMI; dollar | 20% | +1: real yield falling with PMI above 50. -1: real yield rising sharply. | To be completed |
| Trend and momentum | Moving averages; relative strength; breadth | 20% | +1: price above 50- and 200-day averages with improving breadth. -1: below both. | To be completed |
| Sentiment | VIX; AAII survey | 15% | +1: elevated fear with stabilising prices. -1: extreme complacency. | To be completed |

